# Board patch paths, one per line, in application order.
#
# How this file is read (scripts/unixnu/patches.py:12-31):
#   * [kernel] patch_series lists the series files to consult; a series file is
#     read by this one into `plan()`;
#   * a line is skipped when empty or when it starts with '#';
#   * a line is resolved against the profile roots when it begins with
#     "component:" or with a known prefix ("arch:", "soc:", "os:", "device:");
#     otherwise it is resolved relative to this file;
#   * a path that does not exist is a hard error ("patch missing"), a path listed
#     twice is a hard error ("patch appears twice"), and a patch that fails to
#     apply aborts with "XNU patch <path>: ...".
#
# This matters here specifically: the format 1 community repositories carried
# their board patches in patches/xnu-device/*.patch with zzz-prefixed names and
# relied on filename ordering.  Format 2 never looks at file names, so copying
# those patches into a directory would silently do nothing.  Nothing is listed
# below because no board patch has been ported and verified yet; an entry appears
# here only once it applies cleanly to the pinned XNU revision.
#
# Candidates, to be ported one at a time with a test that proves the effect:
#   device:patches/xnu/enchilada-arm64-no-pauth.patch
#       SDM845 is Cortex-A75/A55: no ARMv8.3 pointer authentication, so anything
#       that assumes FEAT_PAuth on arm64 has to be conditionalised.
#   device:patches/xnu/enchilada-smmu-v500.patch
#       apps-smmu is a qsmmu-v500 controller (compatible "qcom,qsmmu-v500",
#       reg 0x15000000+0x80000 with a TCU window at 0x150c2000).  XNU's
#       ArmSmmu4K kit targets MMU-500/4K-style setups and has no qsmmu-v500
#       path, so this is the largest known unknown in the memory area.
